        <mxCell id="KqZPbQY2Lv0Ew4p42Cft-790" parent="KqZPbQY2Lv0Ew4p42Cft-488" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;rounded=0;" value="Notes: &lt;br&gt;1. value column is of type text, another option to add columns for every supported type like text_value, number_value, boolean value, date_value, or a third option is to make the column of json type. Every option has pros and const&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;2. Looking at HIPs 2025 document. field definition should be based on specific hazard not on hazard type. For example; downburst which is classified under metrological hazard type has wind speed metric, but&amp;nbsp;Lightning which is another specific hazard on the hazard type classificiation of downburst has (voltage, current, temperature, speed, and duration) metrics.&lt;br&gt;The relationship here is based on excel sheet to define fields based on hazard type and not based on specific hazard." vertex="1">
